The qualification of welders is based on essential variables. For each essential variable a range of qualification is defined. All test pieces shall be welded using the essential variables independently, except for 5.7 and 5.8. If the welder has to weld outside the range of qualification a new qualification test is required. The essential variables are:

a) welding processes;

b) product type (plate and pipe);

c) type of weld (butt and fillet);

d) material groups;

2) The word "plate" alone or in combination is used to mean "wrought plate" and "flat extruded bars".

3) The word "pipe" alone or in combination, is used to mean "pipe", "tube" or "hollow section".

